@startuml j1-first-visit-and-ask
!include style.iuml
title J1 First visit and ask (the order per message)
actor Patient
participant "Chat page /\n(ChatClient)" as Chat
participant "POST /api/chat" as Api
participant "answer.ts\n(answerPatient)" as Ans
participant "AI provider\n(optional)" as Model
database "Shared store\n(db.ts)" as Store
autonumber

Patient -> Chat : opens /
Chat -> Chat : chat id from local storage, or a new one
Chat -> Api : GET /api/clinic (clinic name for the greeting)
Chat --> Patient : greeting, six quick replies, question box
note right of Chat : a question in the link (?q=) is asked on load

Patient -> Chat : types a question or presses a quick reply
Chat -> Api : POST {chatId, message}
Api -> Store : getClinicData(); insertMessage(user)
note right of Api
A store fault is noted, never thrown: the clinic file
that ships with the app is used and the reply still goes out.
end note
Api -> Ans : answerPatient(message, clinic)
Ans -> Ans : detectLanguage (i18n.ts)
Ans -> Ans : 1 emergency check (guards.ts)
Ans -> Ans : 2 medical-advice and rule-break checks (guards.ts)
Ans -> Ans : 3 booking request? (matcher.ts detectBooking)
alt an AI key is set
  Ans -> Model : 4 one attempt, stopped at 8 seconds, JSON asked for
  Model --> Ans : {found, answer, ...}
  Ans -> Ans : Zod check, then acceptAiReply and keepsFileWording
  note right of Ans
  Rejected: a doctor who is not in the file, a figure for
  another service, a time for another day, a clock time
  without am or pm. A rejected answer goes to step 5.
  "Not found" becomes "not sure" and a needs human ticket.
  end note
end
opt no key, a failed or late call, or a rejected answer
  Ans -> Ans : 5 matchClinicFile (matcher.ts)
  note right of Ans : label "Answered from the clinic file"
end
Ans --> Api : reply, source, label, ticket to open or none
opt a person is needed
  Api -> Store : insertTicket(status, priority, text)
end
Api -> Store : insertMessage(assistant, source)
Api --> Chat : {reply, source, label, ticketId, ticketStatus, stored}
Chat --> Patient : the reply, with the label when it came from the clinic file
@enduml
